[medium] internal/service/relational/suggestions/core.go:136 (correctness)
CanonicalizeFilter collapses duplicate equality conditions by lowercased label key and silently lets the later value win. An existing filter such as AND(env=prod, env=stage) is not equivalent to the single-label set env=stage, but this canonicalization makes mappingExcluded and acceptFilterForHash treat it as a hash match, so suggestions can be excluded or accepted into a dashboard whose real labelfilter does not represent the suggested label set.
Suggested fix: When canonicalizing a condition, check whether the lowercased label key is already present. If it is present with a different value, return false so the filter is not considered canonical; if it is the same value, keep one entry. Add a test covering conflicting duplicate conditions.
Guidance: Fix internal/service/relational/suggestions/core.go in canonicalizeScope. In the condition branch, compute key := strings.ToLower(condition.Label), then check existing, seen := labels[key] before assignment. If seen && existing != condition.Value, return false because AND(env=prod, env=stage) is not equivalent to a single canonical label set. If seen && existing == condition.Value, return true without changing the map. If not seen, assign labels[key] = condition.Value. Preserve the deliberate canonical semantics: lowercase keys only, preserve values exactly, continue accepting duplicate same-key/same-value conditions, and continue rejecting non-'=' operators and non-AND queries. Add tests in internal/service/relational/suggestions/core_test.go: one filter with AND env=prod and Env=stage must make CanonicalizeFilter return ok=false, and one with env=prod and Env=prod must return ok=true with map[string]string{"env":"prod"}. Do not change BuildLabelFilter or CanonicalLabelSetHash.

